{
  "title": "Adopt the shared agent-issues PreToolUse hook",
  "description": "Replace the bespoke Ramekin PreToolUse Python hook with the \
shared agent-pretool-hook runner and a repo-specific declarative \
.agent-issues/pretool-hook.json5 configuration.\n\
\n\
Preserve the existing local guardrails: block raw PR publishing in favor of \
agent-submit, block GitHub Issues, block branch switching without the repo \
signoff env var, prevent manual mutation of generated pipeline output, prefer \
Makefile targets over direct cargo/rustfmt/docker/ramekin-cli invocations \
where the current hook enforces that, and keep dirty generated-output checks \
before publishing. Use agent-issues init --hook for generated scaffolding \
where possible, then remove obsolete bespoke hook code and tests once \
equivalent coverage exists for the shared configuration.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
